{"name":"Crocus Tint","hex":"#fdf1c7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crocus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial flowering plant (of the genus Crocus in the Iridaceae family). Saffron is obtained from the stamens of Crocus sativus.","Any of various similar flowering plants, such as autumn crocus and prairie crocus."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fraudulent doctor; a quack."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crocus"},{"term":"tint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slight coloring.","A pale or faint tinge of any color; especially, a variation of a color obtained by adding white (contrast shade)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shade, to color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crocus","blocks":[{"text":"Crocus is a genus of seasonal flowering plants in the family Iridaceae comprising about 100 species of perennials growing from corms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/860808-Saffronfarm-01-IMG_7707-2.jpg/330px-860808-Saffronfarm-01-IMG_7707-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crocus"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/328_Crocus_sa